//? Title: Neville interpolation: actual triangular updates
//? Subtitle: Original-order cosine prefixes, finite arithmetic and the limits of table differences
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Evaluate an interpolating polynomial at one query without constructing its
coefficients. Actual canonical in-place updates explain a hand-checkable
quadratic example, then retain the original cosine-prefix experiment. A
zero-sample counterexample distinguishes observed agreement from a certified
error estimate, and exact work counts expose the cost of repeated prefix calls.
)

\toc

> Combine overlapping prefix interpolants

Let P_(i..j)(x) interpolate nodes i through j at a fixed query x. Two
overlapping degree-(d−1) interpolants combine as
P_(i..j)=((x−x_i)P_(i+1..j)−(x−x_j)P_(i..j−1))/(x_j−x_i). At each node in their
union the formula reproduces the corresponding y value; its degree is at most d.
Distinct nodes make that polynomial unique, proving the recurrence by induction
from P_(i..i)=y_i.

The native producer initializes p=ys and updates ending indices in descending
order for each increasing degree. Both operands then still belong to the
preceding degree. Reversing that inner order would reuse a newly overwritten
value. The captured records below are its actual operands and assignments, not a
report-side recurrence.

> Three nodes and a hand-checkable square

Nodes−1,0,1 with values1,0,1 interpolate x². At x=.5 the two linear estimates
are−.5 and.5, and the final quadratic gives.25. The final working vector
contains retained mixed-degree entries, not an entire triangular table. Its
three actual update records explain the complete computation.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/neville_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto t = dm::algorithms::neville_trace({-1, 0, 1}, {1, 0, 1}, .5);
    dm::graphics::Diagram d;
    std::print("| actual degree | first node index | last node index | actual right operand | actual left " "operand | committed value |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < t.steps.size(); ++i) {
        auto &s = t.steps[i];
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", s.degree, s.first,
                   s.last, s.right_before, s.left_before, s.value);
        d.node(std::to_string(i),
               {s.degree == 2 ? 7. : 0., s.degree == 2 ? 0. : 3. - 6. * i},
               std::format("Actual P({}..{}) = {}\ndegree {}", s.first, s.last,
                           s.value, s.degree));
    }
    d.edge("0", "2").edge("1", "2");
    d.save_svg("build/neville_tiny.svg");
    std::print("\nActual final value {}; {} recurrence updates.\n",
               t.analysis.value, t.analysis.updates);
}
```
