> Actual work, ownership and complete guards

A complete n-node call makes n(n−1)/2 updates and retains n working values.
Complete pairwise distinctness validation also costs O(n²), so ordinary
evaluation remains O(n²) work and O(n) working storage, including empty and
singleton conventions. Repeating every prefix through n nodes costs O(n³) in
total; it is not one quadratic call. The original seven-node study is a fixed
small instance of that repeated work.

Matched shapes, finite values/query and distinct abscissae are checked
completely. Nodes may be unsorted; literal caller order determines floating
arithmetic. Empty matched inputs retain the historical zero placeholder, not a
data-driven interpolating polynomial. Trace and analyzed calls default to1000000
nodes; ordinary convenience evaluation disables that optional cap. Owned trace
units are exactly1+3n+n(n−1)/2: query, both input vectors, final working values
and actual fixed-size update records. Its separate default1000000-unit quota is
pre-admitted before copying or evaluation; zero disables either policy.

Ordinary finite double operations preserve the legacy recurrence order.
Nonfinite double differences or products use a long-double fallback for that
actual update, including opposite-sign full-width nodes. A final nonfinite
double value throws instead of returning an unchecked infinity or NaN. This
guards representation, not conditioning or mathematical error.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/neville_work.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    std::vector<double> nodes, actual, formula;
    std::print("| input nodes | actual recurrence updates | triangular count | complete trace units |\n| " "---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (int n : {0, 1, 2, 4, 8, 16}) {
        std::vector<double> x(n), y(n);
        std::iota(x.begin(), x.end(), 0.);
        auto t = dm::algorithms::neville_trace(x, y, .5);
        nodes.push_back(n);
        actual.push_back(t.analysis.updates);
        formula.push_back(n * (n - 1) / 2);
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", n, t.analysis.updates,
                   n * (n - 1) / 2, t.captured_entries);
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.lines(nodes, formula, "triangular formula", {192, 59, 50}).points(
        nodes, actual, "actual updates", {36, 105, 172}, 6).title(
        "Neville: actual in-place recurrence work").x_label(
        "complete node count").y_label("actual updates").save_svg(
        "build/neville_work.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| input nodes | actual recurrence updates | triangular count | complete trace units |
| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| 0 | 0 | 0 | 1 |
| 1 | 0 | 0 | 4 |
| 2 | 1 | 1 | 8 |
| 4 | 6 | 6 | 19 |
| 8 | 28 | 28 | 53 |
| 16 | 120 | 120 | 169 |
\image(figures/neville_work.svg)
